{
  "raw": {
    "https://southeast.iu.edu/academics/explore-careers/index.html": {
      "title": "Explore Careers",
      "description": "Career Exploration Indiana University Southeast Indiana University Southeast IU Southeast Skip to Content Skip to Main Navigation Skip to Search Menu Academics Indiana University Southeast Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Academics Explore Careers Explore Careers Take your interests and turn them into a career Discover career possibilities and find the academic path that helps you reach your goals. Whether you are preparing for a specific profession or exploring your interests, IU Southeast offers programs designed to build the knowledge, skills, and experience employers value. Explore career areas that connect your interests with majors, hands-on learning opportunities, and future career pathways. Each area highlights programs that can help you turn your passions into meaningful work. Your future starts with understanding what interests you. Explore each career area to discover majors, opportunities, and pathways that match your goals. Business, leadership, and entrepreneurs Build the skills to lead organizations, solve business challenges, and create new opportunities. Explore majors that prepare you for careers in management, finance, accounting, marketing, entrepreneurship, and more. Healthcare Make a difference in people’s lives through careers focused on health, wellness, and patient care. Discover majors that prepare you for roles in healthcare, mental health, and community wellness. Technology and applied computing Develop the technical skills needed to design solutions and shape the future. Explore programs focused on computing, data informatics, cybersecurity, information systems, and emerging technologies. Communication, media, and creative arts Use creativity and communication to inform, inspire, and connect with others. Find programs that prepare you for careers in media, design, storytelling, music, and the arts. Education, human services, and community impact Support individuals and strengthen communities through service-focused careers. Explore majors that prepare you to teach, advocate, lead, and make a positive impact. Science and the environment Study the natural world while developing skills for discovery, innovation, and sustainability. Explore programs that connect science with careers in research, environmental solutions, and industry. Your Interests. Your Experiences. Your Future. You have interests, goals, and experiences that make you unique. Discover where they could take you at IU Southeast. Take our quick quiz to discover career paths and IU Southeast programs that could be a great fit for you—and see where your future could lead. Career Coach Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Contact, Address and Additional Links Services Canvas One.IU Library AskIU Email About Email at IU Outlook Web Access For Prospective Students Request Information Find Directory Schedule of Classes Map and Directions Academic Calendar Accreditation Faculty and Staff Resources Resources IT Services Bookstore Non-Discrimination Notice University Police Required Disclosures Bad Weather Policy Emergency Information Accessible Educational Services Indiana University Southeast +1-812-941-2333 4201 Grant Line Rd. New Albany, IN 47150 Facebook Flickr Instagram LinkedIn Snapchat Twitter YouTube View the website in Español Accessibility | College Scorecard | Open to All | Privacy Notice | Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University"
    },
    "https://southeast.iu.edu/academics/explore-careers/business-leadership.html": {
      "title": "Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs",
      "description": "Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Indiana University Southeast Indiana University Southeast IU Southeast Skip to Content Skip to Main Navigation Skip to Search Menu Academics Indiana University Southeast Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Academics Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Build the skills to lead, innovate, and shape the future of business Business, leadership, and entrepreneurship careers are driven by problem-solvers, innovators, and professionals who help organizations grow. Whether you want to lead teams, manage resources, launch a business, or help companies adapt in a changing world, IU Southeast programs prepare you with practical knowledge and career-ready skills. Through hands-on learning, industry connections, and real-world experiences, you will develop the communication, critical-thinking, and decision-making skills employers value. Explore programs designed to help you build confidence, discover your strengths, and prepare for a wide range of career opportunities. Create opportunities through business and leadership Successful organizations need professionals who can analyze challenges, develop strategies, and bring ideas to life. Careers in this area span industries and include roles in management, finance, marketing, human resources, operations, entrepreneurship, and more. Students gain experience applying business concepts to real situations through projects, collaboration, and professional-development opportunities. You will learn how to communicate effectively, solve problems, and make informed decisions that create impact. Explore your path in business, leadership, and entrepreneurship Business The highly regarded Bachelor of Science in Business offers you a well-rounded degree that covers the foundations of business. Our degree concentrations offer you a strategic approach to your education, preparing you to succeed in today’s competitive economy, whatever your career goals. Areas of focus Accounting Business Economics and Public Policy Finance General Business General Management Human Resource Management International Business Marketing Professional Selling Supply Chain Management Accounting (100% online) The 100% online B.S. in Accounting is a comprehensive study of the processes and practices of accounting. You’ll learn to think critically and strengthen your decision-making skills that are needed when applying the practices and policies involved in the accounting field and business world. B.S. in Accounting Business Administration (100% online) The online Bachelor of Science in Business Administration (BSBA) gives you a broad foundation in business and managerial principles and prepares for opportunities in multiple job sectors. The program exposes you to core concepts of economics, management, quantitative business analysis, finance, marketing, and information systems. Areas of focus: Accounting Economics Finance Marketing Actuarial Science (100% online) Prepare to analyze risk using mathematics, statistics, and financial theory. This degree equips you for roles in insurance, finance, and corporate planning. B.S. in Actuarial Science Applied Statistics (100% online) Build advanced skills in data analysis, probability, and statistical modeling. You'll be prepared to interpret complex data across a wide range of industries. B.S. in Applied Statistics Tourism, Hospitality, and Event Planning Gain skills in event coordination, travel management, and guest services. This degree offers hands-on experience and industry knowledge for careers in tourism and hospitality. B.S. Tourism, Hospitality, and Event Planning Master of Business Administration Our M.B.A. Your Way program is designed with busy working professionals in mind. Our 8-week classes offer an accelerated completion time, while still allowing you to go at your own pace. We offer flexible scheduling and formats, and convenient locations in New Albany and at the IU Southeast Graduate Center in Jeffersonville, just across the bridge from downtown Louisville. Learn more about the Master of Business Administration degree Concentrations (optional): Accounting Human Resources Management Management Finance Business Data Analytics Master of Science in Management Our Master of Science in Management program can be completed in as little as 12 months, and focuses on the skills required to be a successful manager or leader of an organization in areas such as non-profit, government, healthcare, or for-profit enterprise. MSM Options: General Management (in-person) General Management (100% online) Human Resources (in-person) Human Resources (100% online) Master of Science in Strategic Finance With an M.S.S.F., you’ll learn from expert faculty and industry leaders how to strengthen your skills and abilities in cost management, financial management, business analysis and valuation, financial statement analysis, decision modeling and simulation, and cover topics in fraud and advanced corporate financial strategy. MSSF Options: MSSF Hybrid Program MSSF Online MBA / MSSF Dual Degree Energize your career with a dual M.B.A./M.S.S.F. degree at IU Southeast. Our dual degree program offers a comprehensive skill set that is highly advantageous in today's dynamic business landscape. A dual degree opens doors to upper-level leadership opportunities, offering flexible skills that enhance your marketability in finance, consulting, corporate leadership, and entrepreneurship. Learn more about the MBA / MSSF dual degree Your Interests. Your Experiences. Your Future. You have interests, goals, and experiences that make you unique. Discover where they could take you at IU Southeast. Take our quick quiz to discover career paths and IU Southeast programs that could be a great fit for you—and see where your future could lead. Career Coach Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Contact, Address and Additional Links Services Canvas One.IU Library AskIU Email About Email at IU Outlook Web Access For Prospective Students Request Information Find Directory Schedule of Classes Map and Directions Academic Calendar Accreditation Faculty and Staff Resources Resources IT Services Bookstore Non-Discrimination Notice University Police Required Disclosures Bad Weather Policy Emergency Information Accessible Educational Services Indiana University Southeast +1-812-941-2333 4201 Grant Line Rd. New Albany, IN 47150 Facebook Flickr Instagram LinkedIn Snapchat Twitter YouTube View the website in Español Accessibility | College Scorecard | Open to All | Privacy Notice | Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University"
    },
    "https://southeast.iu.edu/academics/explore-careers/communication-arts.html": {
      "title": "Communication, Media, and Creative Arts",
      "description": "Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Indiana University Southeast Indiana University Southeast IU Southeast Skip to Content Skip to Main Navigation Skip to Search Menu Academics Indiana University Southeast Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Academics Explore Careers Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Tell stories, create connections, and inspire through communication and creativity Communication, media, and creative arts careers help people share ideas, influence audiences, and bring new perspectives to the world. Whether you are interested in storytelling, digital media, visual expression, or strategic communication, IU Southeast programs help you develop the skills to create meaningful work and connect with others. Through hands-on projects, creative experiences, and opportunities to build your portfolio, you will strengthen your communication, collaboration, and problem-solving skills. Explore programs that prepare you for careers where creativity and connection make an impact. Use creativity to shape ideas and engage audiences Today’s organizations need professionals who can communicate clearly, think creatively, and adapt across platforms. Careers in this area include roles in media, journalism, public relations, marketing, design, content creation, music, and the arts. Students gain experience creating projects, developing professional skills, and applying creative strategies to real-world situations. You will learn how to communicate effectively, understand audiences, and use your talents to tell stories that matter. Explore your path in communication, media, and creative arts Discover majors that connect your interests with career opportunities in creative and communication-focused fields. Whether you want to inform communities, develop visual work, produce media, or help organizations share their message, your journey starts here. Explore the programs listed below to find the academic pathway that helps you turn your creativity into a career. Digital Media and Storytelling – Digital Storytelling (100% online) Learn to craft compelling narratives across visual, audio, and digital platforms. This degree emphasizes creativity, media production, and audience engagement in a digital landscape. B.S. Digital Media and Storytelling-Digital Storytelling Digital Media and Storytelling – Public Relations (100% online) Build strategic communication skills for digital-age public relations. This degree focuses on campaign development, brand messaging, and relationship management using modern communication tools. B.S. Digital Media and Storytelling-Public Relations Communication – Organizational Communication Develop effective communication strategies for workplace settings. This degree focuses on leadership, team collaboration, and professional messaging across organizations and industries. B.A. Communication-Organizational Communication B.S. Communication-Organizational Communication Journalism and Media Develop the skills to research, write, create, and share stories across digital, print, broadcast, and emerging media platforms. Gain hands-on experience with media production, communication strategies, and storytelling techniques that prepare you for careers in journalism, content creation, and related fields. B.A. Communication-Journalism and Media B.S. Communication-Journalism and Media Strategic Communication Build expertise in communication planning, public relations, digital media, and audience engagement. Learn how to craft effective messages and develop communication strategies that help organizations connect with their communities and achieve their goals. B.A. Communication-Strategic Communication B.S. Communication-Strategic Communication Sports Leadership Combine communication theory with sports management and leadership. This degree prepares students for roles in athletic administration, media relations, and team coordination. Sports Leadership Music – Audio and Stage Production Learn the technical and artistic elements of sound recording and music production. This degree covers audio engineering, mixing, and studio techniques for music and media. B.S. Music-Audio and Stage Production Music Education – Instrumental P–12 Prepare to teach instrumental music at all grade levels. This degree combines music theory, instrumental performance, and teaching strategies for future music educators. B.S. Music – Music Education – Instrumental P–12 Music Education – Vocal P–12 Train to become a vocal music educator for P–12 students. This degree includes vocal performance, conducting, and music teaching strategies tailored for school settings. B.S. Music – Music Education – Vocal P–12 Spanish – Hispanic Culture, Travel, and Tourism (online) Explore the Spanish-speaking world through the lens of travel, hospitality, and culture. This degree combines language study with practical applications in international tourism. B.S. Spanish-Hispanic Culture, Travel, and Tourism Spanish – Hispanic Cultures in the U.S. (100% online) Focus on the diverse Hispanic communities within the United States. This degree emphasizes language proficiency and cultural literacy in U.S. social and professional contexts. B.S. Spanish-Hispanic Cultures in the U.S. Spanish – Medical Communication (online) Use Spanish in healthcare environments to improve patient communication and care. This degree blends medical terminology with language and cultural studies. B.S. Spanish-Medical Communication Spanish – Spanish for Business (online) Apply Spanish in international and domestic business settings. This degree prepares students for cross-cultural communication in corporate, marketing, or trade-related roles. B.S. Spanish-Spanish for Business Ceramics Explore the expressive and functional possibilities of clay through hands-on studio practice. This degree emphasizes technical proficiency, creative development, and personal artistic voice in ceramic arts. B.F.A. Ceramics Digital Art Combine traditional art foundations with emerging digital tools and techniques. This degree prepares students to create innovative visual work using digital illustration, animation, video, and interactive media. B.F.A. Digital Art Drawing Refine your drawing skills through intensive studio work and conceptual exploration. This degree supports artistic growth through a deep engagement with technique, composition, and personal expression. B.F.A. Drawing Graphic Design Develop visual communication skills through design thinking, typography, branding, and digital media. This degree prepares students for creative careers in advertising, marketing, and digital design industries. B.F.A. Graphic Design Painting Engage deeply with the language of paint through traditional and contemporary approaches. This degree fosters experimentation, critical thinking, and studio mastery to support a personal and professional art practice. B.F.A. Painting Printmaking Explore the art of multiples through techniques like relief, intaglio, lithography, and screen-printing. This degree emphasizes craftsmanship, conceptual development, and interdisciplinary applications in print media. B.F.A. Printmaking Studio Art Develop your artistic voice through immersive studio practice, creative exploration, and professional preparation across a variety of visual disciplines. Build a strong portfolio while learning from experienced faculty and engaging in hands-on projects. B.F.A. Studio Art Applied Science (individualized, online) The Bachelor of Applied Science (BAS) degree at IU Southeast is designed specifically for individuals who have already earned an Associate of Applied Science (AAS) and are looking to take the next step in their professional journey. Our individualized track boosts your AAS in a field other than healthcare or the sciences. The individualized track is highly flexible and allows you to tailor your experience. Individualized Master of Arts in English (100% online) Deepen your understanding of literature, language, and writing with the M.A. in English at IU Southeast. This fully online program is ideal for educators, writers, and professionals seeking advanced skills in literary analysis, composition, and cultural studies. Flexible coursework allows you to tailor your degree to your academic and career goals. M.A. English Your Interests. Your Experiences. Your Future. You have interests, goals, and experiences that make you unique. Discover where they could take you at IU Southeast. Take our quick quiz to discover career paths and IU Southeast programs that could be a great fit for you—and see where your future could lead. Career Coach Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Contact, Address and Additional Links Services Canvas One.IU Library AskIU Email About Email at IU Outlook Web Access For Prospective Students Request Information Find Directory Schedule of Classes Map and Directions Academic Calendar Accreditation Faculty and Staff Resources Resources IT Services Bookstore Non-Discrimination Notice University Police Required Disclosures Bad Weather Policy Emergency Information Accessible Educational Services Indiana University Southeast +1-812-941-2333 4201 Grant Line Rd. New Albany, IN 47150 Facebook Flickr Instagram LinkedIn Snapchat Twitter YouTube View the website in Español Accessibility | College Scorecard | Open to All | Privacy Notice | Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University"
    },
    "https://southeast.iu.edu/academics/explore-careers/education-human-services.html": {
      "title": "Education, Human Services, and Community Impact",
      "description": "Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Indiana University Southeast Indiana University Southeast IU Southeast Skip to Content Skip to Main Navigation Skip to Search Menu Academics Indiana University Southeast Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Academics Explore Careers Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Make a difference through education, service, and community impact Education, human services, and community-focused careers are built around supporting people and strengthening communities. IU Southeast programs prepare you with the knowledge, skills, and experiences needed to help others learn, grow, and thrive. Through hands-on learning, field experiences, and opportunities to work with diverse communities, you will develop strong communication, leadership, and problem-solving skills. Explore programs that prepare you for meaningful careers focused on service, advocacy, and positive change. Support individuals and strengthen communities Professionals in education and human services play an important role in improving lives and creating stronger communities. Careers in this area include teaching, counseling, social services, community programs, public service, and nonprofit work. Students gain real-world experience through practical learning opportunities, collaboration, and community partnerships. You will learn how to understand needs, build relationships, and create solutions that make a lasting impact. Explore your path in education, human services, and community impact Discover majors that connect your interests with careers centered on helping others. From guiding students and supporting families to improving organizations and serving communities, your journey starts here. Explore the programs listed below to find the academic pathway that helps you turn your passion for service into a career. Art Education Prepare to inspire creativity and learning as an art educator through hands-on studio experiences, teaching methods, and classroom-focused training. Build the skills needed to guide students’ artistic development in schools and community settings. B.S. Education-Art Education Elementary Education Prepare to make a difference in the lives of young people with a Bachelor of Science in Elementary Education (B.S.Ed.) degree, where your passion for teaching meets comprehensive, high-quality preparation. Learn more about the B.S. in Education, Elementary Education Concentrations English as a New Language / English as a Second Language (ENL/ESL) Language Arts Mathematics Science Social Studies Special Education Secondary Education Make a difference for young adults today with the Bachelor of Science in Education (B.S.Ed.) Secondary Education program at IU Southeast, where quality teacher education is at the forefront of our mission. Learn more about the B.S. in Education, Secondary Education Concentrations Language Arts Mathematics Science Social Studies History Explore how the past shapes today’s world. Study cultures, politics, and events from ancient civilizations to modern times. Prepare for careers in education, law, government, and beyond. B.A. in History B.S. in History International Studies Gain insight into the cultures, politics, and economies of Africa. Combine language study with international relations for careers in diplomacy, nonprofits, and more. B.A. History- International Studies B.S. History-International Studies Political Science Explore government, politics, and policy at the local, national, and global level. Build skills for careers in law, public service, or advocacy. B.A. in History-Political Science B.S. in History-Political Science Pre-Law Build a strong foundation for legal careers by studying history, government, society, and the forces that shape the law. Develop critical-thinking, research, writing, and analytical skills that prepare you for law school and careers in legal, public service, and policy-related fields. B.A. History-Pre-Law B.S. History-Pre-Law Psychology Study human behavior, cognition, and emotion. Gain research and applied experience for careers in counseling, healthcare, or human services. B.A. in Psychology B.S. Psychology Neuroscience Explore the biological basis of behavior and cognition through interdisciplinary coursework in psychology, biology, and chemistry. Gain research experience and prepare for careers in healthcare, research, or graduate programs in neuroscience and related fields. B.S. Psychology-Neuroscience Criminology and Criminal Justice Study the causes and consequences of crime and the workings of the criminal justice system. Prepare for careers in law enforcement, corrections, forensics, or legal services with a focus on applied knowledge and social responsibility. B.S. in Criminology and Criminal Justice Sociology Explore social structures, inequality, and group behavior. Prepare for careers in research, social work, criminal justice, or community development. B.S. in Criminology-Sociology Social Sciences – Dual Discipline Customize your degree by combining two social science areas, such as psychology and sociology or political science and criminal justice. Strengthen your interdisciplinary skills for flexible career options in education, public service, or business. B.S. in Social Sciences-Dual Discipline Social Sciences – Triple Discipline Design a well-rounded degree with three integrated social science fields. Ideal for students seeking broad expertise and adaptable career pathways in human services, policy, or administration. B.S. in Social Sciences-Triple Discipline Alternate Teacher Licensing Program The Transition to Teaching program at Indiana University Southeast offers an affordable and efficient pathway for you to use your bachelor’s degree in another field to become a licensed teacher. This program is designed to cater to career-changers who are passionate about making a difference in the lives of young students. Early Childhood Program Elementary Program Secondary Program Special Education Program Master of Science in Education with a major in Elementary Education Advance your teaching career with a Master of Science in Education (M.S.Ed.) in Elementary Education from Indiana University Southeast. Our high-quality program is designed to equip you with advanced teaching strategies to engage young minds in diverse classroom settings. Learn more about the M.S.Ed. in Elementary Education Concentrations Educational Leadership ENL / ESL Gifted and Talented Music Education Reading Special Education Technology Master of Science in Education with a major in Secondary Education Move forward in your teaching career at the secondary level with this degree. Our program offers a dynamic pathway for educators seeking advanced credentials. Learn more about the M.S.Ed. in Secondary Education Concentrations Biology Chemistry Composition Studies Educational Leadership English ENL / ESL Gifted and Talented Mathematics Music Education Reading Social Studies Special Education Technology Master of Science in Education with a major in Counseling This program equips graduates with the knowledge and skills necessary to obtain a K–12 school counseling license, preparing them to support the academic, personal, and social development of all students. Learn more about the M.S.Ed. in Counseling Master of Science in Education in Educational Technology for Learning (100% online) This degree is designed for educators and professionals seeking to enhance their expertise in integrating technology into learning environments. Our program prepares graduates to be leaders in educational technology, ready to transform teaching and learning through innovative digital tools and strategies. Learn more about the M.S.Ed. in Educational Technology for Learning Master of Arts in Teaching – French (100% online) Prepare to teach French with confidence. The M.A.T. in French at IU Southeast offers a strong foundation in both language and teaching methods, supporting licensure or advancement in education. Combine your passion for French with practical teaching experience in a flexible hybrid format. M.A.T. French Master of Arts in Teaching – German (100% online) Advance your proficiency in German and gain the pedagogical training needed to teach it effectively. The M.A.T. in German at IU Southeast blends content mastery with teaching methodology, preparing you for licensure or professional roles in language education. M.A.T. German Master of Arts in Teaching in History (100% online) Enhance your expertise in history while gaining teaching licensure or professional development in education. Ideal for current or aspiring educators seeking to teach social studies at the secondary level. M.A.T. History Master of Arts in Teaching in Political Science (100% online) Combine in-depth political science coursework with teacher preparation to strengthen your credentials in social studies education. A great fit for those teaching or planning to teach government and civics. M.A.T. Political Science M.S. in Criminal Justice and Public Safety–Criminal Justice (100% online) Explore criminology theory, criminal law, and justice system practices. This program prepares you for leadership roles in law enforcement, corrections, or criminal justice reform. M.S. Criminal Justice and Public Safety–Criminal Justice M.S. in Criminal Justice and Public Safety–Public Safety (100% online) Focus on emergency management, homeland security, and public policy in this Public Safety track. Prepare for leadership in police, fire, disaster response, and security agencies. M.S. Criminal Justice and Public Safety–Public Safety M.A. in History–American History (100% online) Deepen your understanding of the American past through focused study of its political, cultural, and social evolution. This program prepares you for careers in teaching, research, museums, or government service. M.A. History–American History M.A. in History–World History (100% online) Explore global historical developments and their impact across time and cultures. This degree equips you with advanced research and analytical skills for careers in education, global affairs, and historical scholarship. M.A. History–World History M.A. in Political Science–American Politics (100% online) Analyze U.S. government institutions, political behavior, and public policy with a focus on contemporary issues. Ideal for those pursuing careers in education, advocacy, public service, or law. M.A. Political Science–American Politics M.A. in Political Science–World Politics (100% online) Study global political systems, international relations, and transnational issues through a comparative lens. This program prepares you for careers in international organizations, government, or global nonprofits. M.A. Political Science–World Politics Your Interests. Your Experiences. Your Future. You have interests, goals, and experiences that make you unique. Discover where they could take you at IU Southeast. Take our quick quiz to discover career paths and IU Southeast programs that could be a great fit for you—and see where your future could lead. Career Coach Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Contact, Address and Additional Links Services Canvas One.IU Library AskIU Email About Email at IU Outlook Web Access For Prospective Students Request Information Find Directory Schedule of Classes Map and Directions Academic Calendar Accreditation Faculty and Staff Resources Resources IT Services Bookstore Non-Discrimination Notice University Police Required Disclosures Bad Weather Policy Emergency Information Accessible Educational Services Indiana University Southeast +1-812-941-2333 4201 Grant Line Rd. New Albany, IN 47150 Facebook Flickr Instagram LinkedIn Snapchat Twitter YouTube View the website in Español Accessibility | College Scorecard | Open to All | Privacy Notice | Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University"
    },
    "https://southeast.iu.edu/academics/explore-careers/healthcare.html": {
      "title": "Healthcare",
      "description": "Healthcare Indiana University Southeast Indiana University Southeast IU Southeast Skip to Content Skip to Main Navigation Skip to Search Menu Academics Indiana University Southeast Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Academics Explore Careers Healthcare Build a future in healthcare Healthcare careers continue to grow across hospitals, clinics, laboratories, schools, and community organizations. Whether you want to work directly with patients, support mental health, process medical data, or improve healthcare systems behind the scenes, a healthcare-focused degree can prepare you for a meaningful and stable career path. Why choose a career in healthcare? High-demand field – Jobs in the healthcare industry are in high demand. Make a positive impact – Help people live healthier lives every day. Diverse career paths – From doctors to nurses, techs to therapists, there’s a role for everyone. High-paying career – Healthcare jobs offer competitive salaries and benefits. Explore healthcare careers Direct patient care Nursing Provide direct patient care in hospitals, clinics, schools, and healthcare facilities. Nurses are in high demand and can specialize in areas like pediatrics, emergency care, oncology, and critical care. Mental health and social work Support individuals, families, and communities in overcoming challenges related to mental well-being. Focus on psychology, or continue beyond a bachelor’s degree to specialize in counseling or social work. Indirect patient support Medical laboratory scientist Work behind the scenes of patient care by analyzing blood, tissue, and other laboratory samples that help physicians diagnose and treat disease. IU Southeast has the only Medical Laboratory Science degree in the Kentuckiana region. Health information manager Focus on managing, processing, and distributing healthcare data to support patient care, research, and decision-making. People in this field work with electronic health records and medical databases to ensure accurate and secure healthcare information. Health services coordinator Manage healthcare programs, patient support services, wellness initiatives, and community health efforts in medical and nonprofit organizations. Pre-professional programs IU Southeast offers several pre-professional programs for undergraduate students planning to pursue postgraduate degrees. These programs can be completed with any major. Pre-Med Pre-Physician Assistant Pre-Anesthesiology Assistant Pre-Occupational Therapy Pre-Physical Therapy Pre-Pharmacy Pre-Veterinary Preferred admissions pathways IU Southeast has agreements with several colleges and universities that create preferred admissions pathways to professional programs. Indiana University School of Medicine Evansville Medical Doctor as part of the Bachelor/Medical Doctor Scholarship program Hanover College Doctor of Occupational Therapy Doctor of Physical Therapy Spalding University Master of Science in Athletic Training Doctor of Occupational Therapy Doctor of Physical Therapy Sullivan University Doctor of Pharmacy Healthcare majors Direct Care Nursing Our on-campus, full-time program begins with pre-nursing classes before you can apply to be fully admitted to the nursing program. Experiential learning in our simulation labs is an important part of the education you’ll receive here at IU Southeast. Our challenging program is rigorous, resulting in an exceptional pass rate for the NCLEX-RN. You’ll leave here ready to work in a variety of nursing positions with the skills you need to succeed. B.S. Nursing RN to BSN in-person RN to BSN online Direct Care Clinical Mental Health Counseling Prepare for licensure as a professional counselor with a Master of Arts in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. This program combines academic training with supervised clinical experience to help you support individuals facing emotional, mental, and behavioral challenges. M.A. Clinical Mental Health Counseling Direct Care School Counseling This program equips graduates with the knowledge and skills necessary to obtain a K–12 school counseling license, preparing them to support the academic, personal, and social development of all students. M.S.Ed. in Counseling Direct Care Social Work (via IU Indianapolis) The Master of Social Work (MSW) is a professional graduate program that prepares students for advanced practice in clinical, community, and organizational settings. Graduates are equipped for licensure and ready to lead meaningful change in a variety of social service environments. Master of Social Work Indirect Patient Support Medical Laboratory Science Train in clinical laboratory techniques to support medical diagnoses. The program combines biology, chemistry, and hands-on lab experience. B.S. in Medical Laboratory Science Indirect Patient Support Psychology Study human behavior, cognition, and emotion. Gain research and applied experience for careers in counseling, healthcare, or human services. B.A. in Psychology B.S. Psychology Indirect Patient Support Neuroscience Explore the biological basis of behavior and cognition through interdisciplinary coursework in psychology, biology, and chemistry. Gain research experience and prepare for careers in healthcare, research, or graduate programs in neuroscience and related fields. B.S. Psychology-Neuroscience Indirect Patient Support Health Information Management Manage healthcare data systems, electronic records, and compliance standards. This program blends healthcare knowledge with technology and administration. B.S. in Health Information Management Indirect Patient Support Applied Health Science Our online Applied Health Science degree program is designed for traditional and nontraditional students with previous coursework in pre-nursing (at least 30 hours) who want to explore careers in the larger healthcare field rather than earn a clinical degree. Students choose from two tracks: Community Health Educator or Health Administration. Community Health Educator path Health Administration path Indirect Patient Support Community Health Educator The Nursing Education graduate program allows you to specialize in advanced teaching methods, curriculum development, and assessment strategies, preparing you to become an effective educator in academic settings, healthcare institutions, or clinical settings. You will be ready to use the latest evidence-based practices and pass on your knowledge to the next generation of nursing students, helping them to meet the demands of a dynamic profession. M.S. Nursing-Nursing Education Indirect Patient Support Health Administration The Nursing Administration graduate program prepares nursing professionals to fill key roles in healthcare administration and management. The program combines clinical experience with leadership and organizational management. You’ll learn about strategic management principles, financial management, and organizational behavior, which will prepare you to contribute to the effective and efficient management of healthcare services. M.S. Nursing-Nursing Administration Indirect Patient Support Medical Coding Certificate With career-focused courses, you'll get direct faculty support when you need it. This certificate is complementary to most degree programs and could offer the opportunity for a career path while finishing a 4-year degree at IU Southeast. Medical Coding Certificate Indirect Patient Support Healthcare Documentation Certificate You’ll learn both in-person and online how to transcribe, format, proofread, and edit medical reports dictated by doctors and other professionals. This certificate is complementary to most degree programs and could offer the opportunity for a career path while finishing a 4-year degree at IU Southeast. Healthcare Documentation Certificate Your Interests. Your Experiences. Your Future. You have interests, goals, and experiences that make you unique. Discover where they could take you at IU Southeast. Take our quick quiz to discover career paths and IU Southeast programs that could be a great fit for you—and see where your future could lead. Career Coach Ready to start your healthcare career journey? Let us help you pursue your dream career in healthcare. Undergraduate application Graduate application Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Contact, Address and Additional Links Services Canvas One.IU Library AskIU Email About Email at IU Outlook Web Access For Prospective Students Request Information Find Directory Schedule of Classes Map and Directions Academic Calendar Accreditation Faculty and Staff Resources Resources IT Services Bookstore Non-Discrimination Notice University Police Required Disclosures Bad Weather Policy Emergency Information Accessible Educational Services Indiana University Southeast +1-812-941-2333 4201 Grant Line Rd. New Albany, IN 47150 Facebook Flickr Instagram LinkedIn Snapchat Twitter YouTube View the website in Español Accessibility | College Scorecard | Open to All | Privacy Notice | Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University"
