    "https://southeast.iu.edu/academics/explore-careers/science-environment.html": {
      "title": "Science and the Environment",
      "description": "Science and the Environment Indiana University Southeast Indiana University Southeast IU Southeast Skip to Content Skip to Main Navigation Skip to Search Menu Academics Indiana University Southeast Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community academics/explore-careers Academics Home Academics Explore Careers Science and the Environment Discover, explore, and solve problems through science and the environment Science and environmental careers help us better understand the world and create solutions for the challenges ahead. IU Southeast programs prepare you with the scientific knowledge, research skills, and hands-on experiences needed for careers focused on discovery, innovation, and sustainability. Through laboratory work, field experiences, research opportunities, and collaborative projects, you will develop critical-thinking and problem-solving skills. Explore programs that connect scientific exploration with real-world impact. Study the natural world and shape the future Science professionals help advance knowledge, protect resources, and improve the way we live. Careers in this area include roles in research, environmental science, sustainability, and industry. Students gain experience applying scientific concepts to real challenges through modern learning spaces, faculty-guided projects, and practical experiences. You will learn how to analyze information, investigate questions, and use evidence to make informed decisions. Explore your path in science and the environment Discover majors that connect your curiosity with career opportunities in science, sustainability, and innovation. From studying the planet to exploring new discoveries, your journey starts here. Explore the programs listed below to find the academic pathway that helps you turn your interest in science into a career. Biology Study topics like genetics, evolution, and ecology while developing essential skills in critical thinking, scientific writing, and data analysis. You’ll also gain hands-on experience in research and fieldwork, key for careers or graduate study in biology and related fields. B.A. in Biology Biochemistry Study the chemical processes behind biological systems, including metabolism, enzymes, and DNA. This concentration blends core chemistry with molecular biology to support careers in health, biotech, and research. B.S. Physical Sciences-Biochemistry Chemistry Explore the science behind matter, energy, and chemical reactions through hands-on laboratory experiences and innovative coursework. Develop analytical and problem-solving skills that prepare you for careers in healthcare, research, and industry as well as for graduate study. B.S. Physical Sciences-Chemistry Environmental Chemistry Study the relationship between chemistry and the environment while exploring solutions to real-world challenges like pollution, sustainability, and resource management. Gain practical laboratory and research experience that prepares you for careers focused on environmental protection and scientific discovery. B.S. Physical Sciences-Environmental Chemistry Geosciences Discover the processes that shape our planet through the study of Earth’s systems, natural resources, and environmental change. Build field, laboratory, and analytical skills that support careers in environmental science, sustainability, research, and related fields. B.S. Physical Sciences-Geosciences Physics Investigate the fundamental principles that explain how the universe works, from energy and motion to matter and technology. Build a strong foundation in scientific reasoning, mathematics, and problem-solving for careers in science, engineering, research, and beyond. B.S. Physical Sciences-Physics Physical Sciences Gain a broad foundation in chemistry, physics, and Earth sciences while developing the critical thinking and technical skills needed to understand the natural world. Prepare for diverse career pathways through hands-on learning, research opportunities, and interdisciplinary study. B.A. Physical Sciences Sustainability and Regeneration Explore innovative approaches to protecting natural resources, restoring ecosystems, and creating a more sustainable future. Combine science, environmental knowledge, and problem-solving skills to prepare for careers that address today’s environmental challenges. B.S. Physical Sciences - Sustainability and Regeneration Sustainability Studies (online) Connect with real-world sustainability challenges, preparing you to apply sustainable practices in businesses, government agencies, and nonprofits. B.A. in Sustainability Studies Your Interests. Your Experiences. Your Future. You have interests, goals, and experiences that make you unique. Discover where they could take you at IU Southeast. Take our quick quiz to discover career paths and IU Southeast programs that could be a great fit for you—and see where your future could lead. Career Coach Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Contact, Address and Additional Links Services Canvas One.IU Library AskIU Email About Email at IU Outlook Web Access For Prospective Students Request Information Find Directory Schedule of Classes Map and Directions Academic Calendar Accreditation Faculty and Staff Resources Resources IT Services Bookstore Non-Discrimination Notice University Police Required Disclosures Bad Weather Policy Emergency Information Accessible Educational Services Indiana University Southeast +1-812-941-2333 4201 Grant Line Rd. New Albany, IN 47150 Facebook Flickr Instagram LinkedIn Snapchat Twitter YouTube View the website in Español Accessibility | College Scorecard | Open to All | Privacy Notice | Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University"
    },
    "https://southeast.iu.edu/academics/explore-careers/technology-computing.html": {
      "title": "Technology and Applied Computing",
      "description": "Technology and Applied Computing Indiana University Southeast Indiana University Southeast IU Southeast Skip to Content Skip to Main Navigation Skip to Search Menu Academics Indiana University Southeast Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Academics Explore Careers Technology and Applied Computing Shape the future through technology, innovation, and problem-solving Technology and applied computing careers are transforming the way people live, work, and connect. Whether you are interested in developing software, processing data, protecting information, or creating digital solutions, IU Southeast programs help you build the technical skills and knowledge needed for today’s evolving workforce. Through hands-on learning, practical experiences, and opportunities to apply concepts to real-world challenges, you will strengthen your problem-solving, analytical, and creative-thinking skills. Explore programs that prepare you for careers where technology meets innovation and impact. Create solutions through computing and technology Technology professionals help organizations operate, improve, and adapt in a digital world. Careers in this area include roles in software development, cybersecurity, data analysis, information systems, programming, and emerging technologies. Students gain experience using current tools, solving complex problems, and developing solutions that meet real needs. You will learn how to think critically, collaborate with others, and apply technology to improve communities, businesses, and industries. Explore your path in technology and applied computing Discover majors that connect your interests with career opportunities in a growing field. Whether you want to build technology, protect digital systems, analyze information, or use data to drive decisions, your journey starts here. Explore the programs listed below to find the academic pathway that helps you turn your curiosity into a career. Cybersecurity Learn to protect digital systems from threats through secure design and defense strategies. You'll study ethical hacking, risk assessment, and cyber law. B.S. in Computer Science-Cybersecurity Information Systems Combine computing knowledge with business applications to improve organizational performance. Coursework emphasizes databases, networks, and system design. B.S. in Computer Science-Information Systems Informatics Explore how technology, data, and people work together to improve systems and solve problems. Gain experience with programming, data management, and digital tools that prepare you for careers in information technology, analytics, and technology-driven fields. B.S. Computer Science-Informatics (in-person) B.S. Computer Science-Informatics (online) Data Science (100% online) Master data collection, visualization, and analysis techniques to uncover meaningful insights. You'll work with big data tools and machine learning technologies. B.S. in Data Science Your Interests. Your Experiences. Your Future. You have interests, goals, and experiences that make you unique. Discover where they could take you at IU Southeast. Take our quick quiz to discover career paths and IU Southeast programs that could be a great fit for you—and see where your future could lead. Career Coach Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Contact, Address and Additional Links Services Canvas One.IU Library AskIU Email About Email at IU Outlook Web Access For Prospective Students Request Information Find Directory Schedule of Classes Map and Directions Academic Calendar Accreditation Faculty and Staff Resources Resources IT Services Bookstore Non-Discrimination Notice University Police Required Disclosures Bad Weather Policy Emergency Information Accessible Educational Services Indiana University Southeast +1-812-941-2333 4201 Grant Line Rd. New Albany, IN 47150 Facebook Flickr Instagram LinkedIn Snapchat Twitter YouTube View the website in Español Accessibility | College Scorecard | Open to All | Privacy Notice | Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University"
    },
    "https://southeast-iu.lightcastcc.com/?radius=&region=Louisville%20Metro": {
      "title": "Welcome to Career Coach",
      "description": "Career Coach - Welcome to Career Coach Cookie Policy This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience on our website. Lightcast's Privacy Policy Decline Allow cookies skip to main content Search Login Sign Up Interests Careers Programs Résumé Builder Welcome to Career Coach Discover majors and in-demand careers and education based on your interests! Find the path that's right for you Interests Uncover your interests and learn how they connect to careers and education. Match My Interests How It Works Inventory Your Interests Use Interests to identify your traits Explore Your Career Options View detailed information about careers matched to your interests Find Education Options Discover an educational path to a selected career Find hot careers in your region Start exploring high paying and growing careers. Loading... See More Hot Careers Explore career options on your own Start your search with one of these options Browse Careers Browse or search for careers and we will give you relevant data on wages, employment, and the training you need. Or Browse All Careers Browse Programs Browse or search for the available Programs that lead to the career you want. Or Browse All Programs Build a résumé to apply to work Our easy-to-use résumé builder will help you create a professional résumé. Start Building Your Résumé We give students the skills they need to be competitive in today's economy. We share a vision of a better future by exemplifying exceptional leadership, advocacy and support on behalf of the community colleges. Our mission is to make you as successful as possible. Connect With Us Career Coach is powered by privacy policy | o*net information | disclaimer | status | cookie consent | © copyright 2026. all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=&sl=en&tl=es&u=southeast.iu.edu/academics/explore-careers/index.html": {
      "title": "Explore Careers",
      "description": "Career Exploration Indiana University Southeast Indiana University Southeast IU Southeast Skip to Content Skip to Main Navigation Skip to Search Menu Academics Indiana University Southeast Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Admissions Apply Now Academics Students Athletics News & Events Alumni & Giving About Southeast Community Home Academics Explore Careers Explore Careers Take your interests and turn them into a career Discover career possibilities and find the academic path that helps you reach your goals. Whether you are preparing for a specific profession or exploring your interests, IU Southeast offers programs designed to build the knowledge, skills, and experience employers value. Explore career areas that connect your interests with majors, hands-on learning opportunities, and future career pathways. Each area highlights programs that can help you turn your passions into meaningful work. Your future starts with understanding what interests you. Explore each career area to discover majors, opportunities, and pathways that match your goals. Business, leadership, and entrepreneurs Build the skills to lead organizations, solve business challenges, and create new opportunities. Explore majors that prepare you for careers in management, finance, accounting, marketing, entrepreneurship, and more. Healthcare Make a difference in people’s lives through careers focused on health, wellness, and patient care. Discover majors that prepare you for roles in healthcare, mental health, and community wellness. Technology and applied computing Develop the technical skills needed to design solutions and shape the future. Explore programs focused on computing, data informatics, cybersecurity, information systems, and emerging technologies. Communication, media, and creative arts Use creativity and communication to inform, inspire, and connect with others. Find programs that prepare you for careers in media, design, storytelling, music, and the arts. Education, human services, and community impact Support individuals and strengthen communities through service-focused careers. Explore majors that prepare you to teach, advocate, lead, and make a positive impact. Science and the environment Study the natural world while developing skills for discovery, innovation, and sustainability. Explore programs that connect science with careers in research, environmental solutions, and industry. Your Interests. Your Experiences. Your Future. You have interests, goals, and experiences that make you unique. Discover where they could take you at IU Southeast. Take our quick quiz to discover career paths and IU Southeast programs that could be a great fit for you—and see where your future could lead. Career Coach Register for Classes Before You Register When to Register Drop & Add Classes Colleges Degrees and Majors Student Experience Academic Advising Register for Classes Bulletin Explore Careers Business, Leadership and Entrepreneurs Communication, Media, and Creative Arts Education, Human Services, and Community Impact Healthcare Science and the Environment Technology and Applied Computing Contact, Address and Additional Links Services Canvas One.IU Library AskIU Email About Email at IU Outlook Web Access For Prospective Students Request Information Find Directory Schedule of Classes Map and Directions Academic Calendar Accreditation Faculty and Staff Resources Resources IT Services Bookstore Non-Discrimination Notice University Police Required Disclosures Bad Weather Policy Emergency Information Accessible Educational Services Indiana University Southeast +1-812-941-2333 4201 Grant Line Rd. New Albany, IN 47150 Facebook Flickr Instagram LinkedIn Snapchat Twitter YouTube View the website in Español Accessibility | College Scorecard | Open to All | Privacy Notice | Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University"
    }
